{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian","id":1335692,"title":"Most interesting Antediluvian","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-14T02:51:54-07:00","id":1335692,"title":"Most interesting Antediluvian","content":"Who do think is the most interesting? Which clan founder fascinates you the most? <br /> <br /> Haqim is my choice. Most badass antediluvian. Love the Web of Knives origin story. It could also make for an interesting premise He could be Caine's greatest failure, his eternal rival, the torn in his side. The one that butchered his first children and stole his blood and has been hunting him and the rest of his kin throughout the ages. <br /> <br /> He also has a link with the baali through Ur-Shulgi and might have a interesting connection with the other great badass, Saulot. Both were actively involved in the baali wars and Saulot seems to have a certain respect for Haqim. In one story he asked him to be the judge of the second city because he didn't think any other vampire could keep his brothers and sisters of the 3rd generation in line. Or maybe Saulot just wanted to keep the ante that worried him the most close to him. Gain his trust by offering him this position, so he could stab him in the back later. There is also the line somewhere of Haqim not trusting Saulot. Some interesting stuff is going on between these two.<br /> <br /> There is also the mythical conversation he had with Mithras before disappearing that fascinates me. It could make for a good story in itself.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T03:13:28-07:00","id":1335693,"title":"","content":"All \u201cAntediluvians(Cainites before the Flood)\u201d are interesting.<br /> <br /> Well, more specifically,<br /> <br /> All 2nd Gens(1st-4th editions don\u2019t leave much room for them because they are assumed \u201clong gone\u201d (and it\u2019s true)). But I expect to see them more active in 5E, Enoch of BJD may imply they are the true patrons of Jyhad and change the theme of it.<br /> Saulot<br /> The Eldest<br /> Arikel<br /> Ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 09-14-2019, 06:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T08:45:52-07:00","id":1335732,"title":"","content":"She doesn't hunt. Humans and vampire alike are lined up outside her door waiting to be fed from.<br /> <br /> She doesn't need to read books, because they are all about her in some way or another.<br /> <br /> Her clan is so edgy and so powerful, it makes the Ventrue seem like the Rotary Club.<br /> <br /> When she pays a boon, markets crash worldwide.<br /> <br /> When she wants to eat al fresco, she turns a river to blood.<br /> <br /> She is: The Most Interesting Antediluvian In The World.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I don't always drink vitae, but when I do, I prefer my descendants.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T11:50:30-07:00","id":1335759,"title":"","content":"Maybe Malkav, just because I've always been curious what it was that broke her mind and soul so badly.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T12:39:28-07:00","id":1335769,"title":"","content":"Every single one of them have something of interest, it is really hard to choose one over the others.<br /> <br /> [Brujah] / Troile. Both sire and childe their relationship is remarkably interesting, one being cold and calculating and the other being the exact opposite, yet both impossibly wise scholars.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius' conviction to diablerize God always fascinated me because I doubt he was wrong on that one, yet it intrigues me his move of letting himself be diablerized by Augustus, what was the purpose of it? I doubt it to be hubris, but somehow I believe it was a sliver of conscience or remorse attempting himself to stop becoming God because he could actually become it and so he foiled his own plans on purpose.<br /> <br /> [Lasombra]'s origin in his interests in the Abyss, what drove him to investigate it in the first place and how did he actually achieve to drive its essence into a discipline?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-14T19:54:27-07:00","id":1335826,"title":"","content":"I always had a soft spot for a number of the 'Alternate' Antediluvians presented in Gehenna. Especially the Shaper. The idea you could have ancient vampires still wandering around and NOT doing dickish things (as far as we know) until circumstances forced them to was rather interesting to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T02:04:37-07:00","id":1335854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1335769#post1335769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every single one of them have something of interest, it is really hard to choose one over the others.<br /> <br /> [Brujah] / Troile. Both sire and childe their relationship is remarkably interesting, one being cold and calculating and the other being the exact opposite, yet both impossibly wise scholars.<br /> <br /> Cappadocius' conviction to diablerize God always fascinated me because I doubt he was wrong on that one, yet it intrigues me his move of letting himself be diablerized by Augustus, what was the purpose of it? I doubt it to be hubris, but somehow I believe it was a sliver of conscience or remorse attempting himself to stop becoming God because he could actually become it and so he foiled his own plans on purpose.<br /> <br /> [Lasombra]'s origin in his interests in the Abyss, what drove him to investigate it in the first place and how did he actually achieve to drive its essence into a discipline?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of them are interesting but of the ones you mentionend, i am the most fascinated by [Lasombra]. Mainly because of what happend (or didn't happen) during the assault on his castle. The mysteries surounding that night and whether or not he was actually diablrized is very interesting. He is also in my mind the most evil ante. Even someone like Tzimisce still cared about one of his childer. [Lasombra] on the other hand probably doesnt have a shred of kindness left in him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T06:17:42-07:00","id":1335876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1335854#post1335854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of them are interesting but of the ones you mentionend, i am the most fascinated by [Lasombra]. Mainly because of what happend (or didn't happen) during the assault on his castle. The mysteries surounding that night and whether or not he was actually diablrized is very interesting. He is also in my mind the most evil ante. Even someone like Tzimisce still cared about one of his childer. [Lasombra] on the other hand probably doesnt have a shred of kindness left in him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I would be entirely fine with not being the recipient of an abyss god's idea of kindness...<br /> <br /> I do quite like Lasombra. Not as much as Tzimisce - that thing is my favourite Ante - but I'm curious moreso as to why Lasombra decided his Clan were gonna be a bunch of seafarers and pirates.<br /> <br /> As for the Anarch Revolt, if the revolutionaries couldn't even take out the majority of Elders (as evidenced by the fact they were in any position to just say &quot;the Camarilla is in charge now&quot; and half the revolutionaries fell in line) I do not for believe for even a second that they took out Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25611,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","user":"GilbyTheFat","date":". 09-15-2019, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T12:32:59-07:00","id":1335935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1335854#post1335854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of them are interesting but of the ones you mentionend, i am the most fascinated by [Lasombra]. Mainly because of what happend (or didn't happen) during the assault on his castle. The mysteries surounding that night and whether or not he was actually diablrized is very interesting. He is also in my mind the most evil ante. Even someone like Tzimisce still cared about one of his childer. [Lasombra] on the other hand probably doesnt have a shred of kindness left in him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah [Lasombra] is extremely interesting. I do believe that he transcended cainite form and is purely an abyssal entity or he is the abyss itself. Yet there is one thing that is intriguing about the clan. Montano being the eldest he is merely 3000 years, therefore, there is a void of Lasombra cainites in vampire history from the Second City to 1600 BC. I believe that [Lasombra] killed the entire clan prior to Montano's embrace.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:26:14-07:00","id":1335943,"title":"","content":"Well, I think it was the clan novels hinted that Lasombra wiped or changed his childers earliest memories... and that Montano was a physical type that does not exist any more, the species having changed since his embrace.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Tubal Cain was said to be the first metalsmith and a mortal descendant of Caine, the son of Lamech and Zillah. Josephus suggested he was the inventor of bronze, while T. C. Mitchell believes him to have discovered cold-forging copper which would be much further back. His bible entry places him much further back in time than Elimelech at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:35:22-07:00","id":1335945,"title":"","content":"Whoever it was that sired the first 3 Baali.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T04:17:36-07:00","id":1336017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1335943#post1335943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think it was the clan novels hinted that Lasombra wiped or changed his childers earliest memories... and that Montano was a physical type that does not exist any more, the species having changed since his embrace.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Tubal Cain was said to be the first metalsmith and a mortal descendant of Caine, the son of Lamech and Zillah. Josephus suggested he was the inventor of bronze, while T. C. Mitchell believes him to have discovered cold-forging copper which would be much further back. His bible entry places him much further back in time than Elimelech at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally forgot about Tubal-Cain. So there might be a lasombra methuselah older then Montano afterall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 09-16-2019, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T04:18:14-07:00","id":1336018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1335945#post1335945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whoever it was that sired the first 3 Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Saulot then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T05:13:22-07:00","id":1336026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336018#post1336018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Saulot then</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> + Haqim and probably Tzimisce (and maybe even Cappadocius)<br /> <br /> V20 changed much of the original approach to the Baali origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-16-2019, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T07:36:24-07:00","id":1336035,"title":"","content":"Saulot certainly is quiet interesting and multi faceted.<br /> <br /> Also Lasombras set up, his diablerie? and whats up with Montano, Gratiano etc., is quiet interesting. Though the pay of so far (his appearance in End Times etc.) has been quiet lack luster.<br /> <br /> I like the Eldest, but it is probably the most well explained and fleshed out of the Antediluvians which takes away some of the mystery surrounding them.<br /> <br /> There is something to be said for those more shrouded in mystery like Arikel, Ventru (if you think it is not dead) and also Ravnos (depending of your stance on the week of nightmares) little is known about their goals, motives and what they were up to beyond ancient times and their clans have a propensity for disciplines that gives them great potential to influence thing subtly from afar.<br /> All of which makes me want to know more about them, and gives STs great leeway to do with them as they want.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T07:57:42-07:00","id":1336040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336035#post1336035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also Lasombras set up, his diablerie?</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the Lasombra just straight-up lied.<br /> <br /> I always found their conduct suspicious. The Lasombra are a Clan who are so callous and powerhungry that they would be the most likely to sit back and let the other Clans get wiped out. And yet after telling everyone they killed their Antediluvian they join up with a Sect which is about saving all Kindred to help hunt down and kill the Antediluvians that <i>wouldn't</i> be able to affect the Lasombra?<br /> <br /> That was a cute lie while it lasted, Clan Lasombra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T08:35:17-07:00","id":1336048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336040#post1336040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Lasombra just straight-up lied.<br /> <br /> I always found their conduct suspicious. The Lasombra are a Clan who are so callous and powerhungry that they would be the most likely to sit back and let the other Clans get wiped out. And yet after telling everyone they killed their Antediluvian they join up with a Sect which is about saving all Kindred to help hunt down and kill the Antediluvians that <i>wouldn't</i> be able to affect the Lasombra?<br /> <br /> That was a cute lie while it lasted, Clan Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div> True, but then that has always been more of a problem of the clusterfuck of mismatched ideas that is the Sabbat. The Lasombra as a Clan appear to be super hierarchical and tightly controlled, why are they founders of the Sabbat and not the Camarilla (well in the same way, take away the historical metaplot and then ask me which 2 calns would most likely worship their founder and try to recreate themselves in his image, my answer would be Tzimisce and Lasombra. They certainly wouldn't be the first Clans I pic for kill their Antediluvian)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25507-nobby","name":"nobby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T08:48:22-07:00","id":1336050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nobby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336048#post1336048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but then that has always been more of a problem of the clusterfuck of mismatched ideas that is the Sabbat. The Lasombra as a Clan appear to be super hierarchical and tightly controlled, why are they founders of the Sabbat and not the Camarilla (well in the same way, take away the historical metaplot and then ask me which 2 calns would most likely worship their founder and try to recreate themselves in his image, my answer would be Tzimisce and Lasombra. They certainly wouldn't be the first Clans I pic for kill their Antediluvian)</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's not forget that, also, the Book of Nod - that text the Sabbat love to ramble on about - revers the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven Clans that founded the Camarilla. Nothing for the two Clans of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, we could go with the option of saying &quot;the Book of Nod is outdated&quot; but considering the emphasis the later books - lots of them - put on the Sabbat and detailing them, and the number of books they did revised versions of...<br /> <br /> The Sabbat truly is the most clustered of fucks if they're going to revere a text which was written by an Antediluvian (IIRC, Saulot wrote it) and reveres the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven enemy Clans. Not that they read the bloody thing, evidently, since I recall the Book of Nod containing things such as &quot;Caine said not to worship him&quot; and &quot;do not consume the heart's blood&quot; and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T09:25:03-07:00","id":1336058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336050#post1336050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that, also, the Book of Nod - that text the Sabbat love to ramble on about - revers the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven Clans that founded the Camarilla. Nothing for the two Clans of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, we could go with the option of saying &quot;the Book of Nod is outdated&quot; but considering the emphasis the later books - lots of them - put on the Sabbat and detailing them, and the number of books they did revised versions of...<br /> <br /> The Sabbat truly is the most clustered of fucks if they're going to revere a text which was written by an Antediluvian (IIRC, Saulot wrote it) and reveres the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven enemy Clans. Not that they read the bloody thing, evidently, since I recall the Book of Nod containing things such as &quot;Caine said not to worship him&quot; and &quot;do not consume the heart's blood&quot; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am of the mind that the Book of Nod was edited to remove the words of the elders, making them apocryphal (much similar to what was done with the &quot;Lost&quot; gospels).<br /> <br /> If so, who did it, and to what purpose?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T09:29:18-07:00","id":1336059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raunalyn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336058#post1336058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am of the mind that the Book of Nod was edited to remove the words of the elders, making them apocryphal (much similar to what was done with the &quot;Lost&quot; gospels).<br /> <br /> If so, who did it, and to what purpose?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the same folks who said they're against slavery and then decided to implement the Vaulderie, while admitting the likes of the Salubri Warriors and Harbingers of Skulls whose sole motive of avenging their Antediluvians is both against the Antediluvian-killing doctrine and a violation of the Code of Milan saying &quot;don't use the Sabbat for personal agendas and gain.&quot; #integrity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T11:59:25-07:00","id":1336071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GilbyTheFat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336050#post1336050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not forget that, also, the Book of Nod - that text the Sabbat love to ramble on about - revers the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven Clans that founded the Camarilla. Nothing for the two Clans of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I mean, we could go with the option of saying &quot;the Book of Nod is outdated&quot; but considering the emphasis the later books - lots of them - put on the Sabbat and detailing them, and the number of books they did revised versions of...<br /> <br /> The Sabbat truly is the most clustered of fucks if they're going to revere a text which was written by an Antediluvian (IIRC, Saulot wrote it) and reveres the words of the Antediluvians of six of the seven enemy Clans. Not that they read the bloody thing, evidently, since I recall the Book of Nod containing things such as &quot;Caine said not to worship him&quot; and &quot;do not consume the heart's blood&quot; and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, the Sabbat would work much better as an Antediluvian-worshipping Gehenna cult seeking to bring about the apocalypse. The role of <i>'elder-killing rebellous neonates who give the finger to the rules</i>' should obviously go to the Anarchs (especially after the nice, Carthian-like redisign they got in the V20 books).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T12:09:16-07:00","id":1336072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336071#post1336071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the Sabbat would work much better as an Antediluvian-worshipping Gehenna cult seeking to bring about the apocalypse. The role of <i>'elder-killing rebellous neonates who give the finger to the rules</i>' should obviously go to the Anarchs (especially after the nice, Carthian-like redisign they got in the V20 books).</div> </div> </div> </div>An alternative option could be that the Sabbat would have worked much better as an Antediluvian-worshipping conspiracy who want to return the world to the &quot;good ol' nights&quot; when Kindred openly ruled and the cattle quivered, bowed and offered their necks in hopes that when a Kindred inflicts their cruelty and hunger upon the living its upon someone else.<br /> <br /> &quot;Look at what the Masquerade has done to our world! We used to be the glorious overlords! The eldest of our lines used to be worshipped as <i>Gods!</i> But now mankind has spent so long thinking it should bow to nobody that it would take up arms against us, and it is un-fucking-becoming!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T01:24:46-07:00","id":1336167,"title":"","content":"I like all of them, but probably, the most detailed and complex are the ones depicted in the Transilvania and Giovanni books (Saulot, the Eldest, Tremere, Ashur, etc.) I also like the alternative antediluvians of the Gehenna scenario : the mysterious Mekhet, the beautiful Lucien, Lilith, etc. I like the idea that there were far more than 13 clans in the second city, although most of them are extinct now, some of the bloodlines could be remnants of these ancient progenitors. Of them, I really like Illyes, the time lord, probably the first in being destroyed or use their disappearance to play the Jyhad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T07:01:16-07:00","id":1336200,"title":"","content":"I really like Saulot, and the various takes on him. I am inclined to believe that he is not &quot;Evil&quot; per se, but that he is actively looking to destroy the Curse of Caine by bringing about Gehenna, but only in that all vampires are destroyed, but not humanity.<br /> <br /> The other Antediluvian I think may have everyone fooled is Capadocius...I don't think he is gone. In fact, in my games, the reason why he allowed Uncle Augie to diablerize him is so that he could remove himself from the great Jyhad, letting everyone believe he was destroyed. That way, he could continue his plans unrestricted. Well, his Wraith could. Or, maybe not his Wraith, but his Spectre. Oh, Uncle Augie is acting weird? How would someone notice with a being so old and eccentric...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24575-raunalyn","name":"Raunalyn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T09:34:11-07:00","id":1336226,"title":"","content":"I retain a soft spot for Saulot despite the obvious changes he's gone under (and the different opinions about whether the retconning was good or bad. If nothing else I at least admire the efforts to tie it all together and consider it an interesting puzzle to play with.)<br /> <br /> I also had more of a sympathetic view on Haqim, even despite stuff like Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> I never gained much enthusiasm for Tzimisce and the whole Vissictude thing, especially with how it was handled in Gehenna. It always felt like someone had played too much Halo and decided 'VAMPIRE FLOOD! GREAT IDEA!' Or maybe it's a remnant of my dissatisfaction from the old 'Alien Plague' theory on Vissictude.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I had less of a problem with Lasombra and Obtenebration despite being essentially the same thing. Although I always had more of a Lovecraftian vibe from that (more an implied threat rather than 'Spacegod comes to earth and destroys us' which is also kinda what we saw of Lasombra in Gehenna.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 09-17-2019, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T14:06:42-07:00","id":1336303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336226#post1336226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I retain a soft spot for Saulot despite the obvious changes he's gone under (and the different opinions about whether the retconning was good or bad. If nothing else I at least admire the efforts to tie it all together and consider it an interesting puzzle to play with.)<br /> <br /> I also had more of a sympathetic view on Haqim, even despite stuff like Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> I never gained much enthusiasm for Tzimisce and the whole Vissictude thing, especially with how it was handled in Gehenna. It always felt like someone had played too much Halo and decided 'VAMPIRE FLOOD! GREAT IDEA!' Or maybe it's a remnant of my dissatisfaction from the old 'Alien Plague' theory on Vissictude.<br /> <br /> Oddly, I had less of a problem with Lasombra and Obtenebration despite being essentially the same thing. Although I always had more of a Lovecraftian vibe from that (more an implied threat rather than 'Spacegod comes to earth and destroys us' which is also kinda what we saw of Lasombra in Gehenna.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A man after my heart. Like you i retain a soft spot for Saulot and Haqim. Never liked Tzimisce that much but somehow i liked Lasombra eventhough they are kinda similair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T06:33:52-07:00","id":1336541,"title":"","content":"I would vote for Saulot I think... although Cappadocius would be a close second. <br /> <br /> I have my own cannon explanation for all the antediluvians and where they are now (As of 2005 where my campaign is currently set)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12180-jeevesosiris","name":"Jeevesosiris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T07:13:16-07:00","id":1336549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeevesosiris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336541#post1336541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would vote for Saulot I think... although Cappadocius would be a close second.<br /> <br /> I have my own cannon explanation for all the antediluvians and where they are now (As of 2005 where my campaign is currently set)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well now you have me curious. What is your cannon explanation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:02:43-07:00","id":1336571,"title":"","content":"Tremere<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bANCIENT: I have lived\u2026 No. I have existed for<br /> over a thousand years, and that is a great deal of time<br /> to ponder one\u2019s actions. Most of all, I dwell upon the<br /> fortunes that brought me to this. If I had any cause left<br /> to believe that Hell had power over me, I might fear<br /> for my decrepit soul. More than anyone else, I can<br /> appreciate the chains of the flesh and the yearning to<br /> escape upward.<br /> I knew full well what would happen when I drank<br /> that potion, brewed from the blood of a monster. I knew<br /> even then that I sentenced my Daemon to death, that<br /> I would lose my magic and be forever outcast from the<br /> light of day. Oh yes, I knew the consequences of my<br /> actions. However, I knew the mysteries of Fate also,<br /> child. The secrets of the Ars Fati were no less compelling<br /> in my day than in yours. When the vis began to die,<br /> I, like many others, looked to the mysteries contained<br /> in unraveling threads. What we discovered, all of us,<br /> pleased no one. The cowardly retreated from the world.<br /> The proud denied the truth until it ground them underfoot.<br /> The brave perished, raging against the turning of<br /> Fortune\u2019s Wheel. The resourceful? You look now upon<br /> the last of them.<br /> I have outlived many enemies. I have deceived<br /> Death. I have cheated even the fall of magic. I have<br /> usurped the legacy of the First Murderer and supped on<br /> souls until my own empty heart grew heavy with the<br /> echoes of their anguish. Who, or what, speaks through<br /> you, child, that I who may yet see the unmaking of<br /> Time, hear in your words that distant stirring of the<br /> mystic sight I and my kind murdered a millennium ago?<br /> Who, or what, indeed?<br /> I am old and tired, and perhaps it will come to<br /> pass one day soon that Fate cuts down the monster it<br /> has made. However, until such a day, I have my own<br /> responsibilities. So hear me, Gilmore \u2014 press this matter<br /> at your own risk. For there are worse fates than death,<br /> and better enemies to fight\u2026 are there not? </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because unlike the others he is not perfect: his plans may be flawed, he still is full of hyubris, but then again he is still human in some regards. The others antes are far too alien, too perfect.<br /> He is probably the most ambitious characters in the history of the world of Darkness. Sure, sometimes plans backfire, but it is inevitable when you decide to shoot for the moon.<br /> <br /> <br /> He was the weakest among the 12 archmages who founded the Order of Hermes. He lacked Tytalus martial prowess or Bonisagus intellect. But where are the others?<br /> Of the the founders only he survives to the present day.<br /> Where is Bonisagus with all of his mastery, and Tempus Flambeux with his fiery rage?<br /> <br /> Mistridge is ancient history, Doissetep has fallen, Horizon pillaged like some village, House Jannissaries is no more, Mercury has been conquered by the Nephandi , Porthos is dead, Mustai too, Avis Malone is gone, the old masters succumbed to history, and yet he stands. Always worse than before, always with something less, and something more. The ultimate survivor.<br /> <br /> The weakest among the archmages, and yet he skyrocketed himself at the top of the order, going very close to control it all.<br /> And then, when he understood that magic was diyng and how meaningless the Order would have become he decided to step into a different game: he crashed like a meteor in the world of the vampires; stood his own against the rest of the Order of Hermes and he almost drove it to extinction, while the Clan Tremere rose to become probably the most powerful Clan in the world of Darkness. He is the first to diablerize an Antidiluvian, and with better results than Augustus, Gratiano or Lugoj.<br /> Augustus, Gratiano, Lugoj, no one of them become a real player of the Jyhad: Tremere did.<br /> <br /> Sure, Saulot had quite the role in all of this, but even Saulot's plan backfired, since he didn't imagined how strong the will of Tremere would have been. I'm sure Saulot would have do without being trapped in a mental battle for 800 years.<br /> He is the only human that managed to sit at the table of the Jyhad if not as an equal of the Antes, then surely as a dangerous upstart. He is the only true new player in a game that didn't had new players since the Second City.<br /> Maybe he fares worse than some : yeah, maybe Saulot, Tzimisce and Lasombra are doing better, but no doubt Tremere he is doing better than Ravnos, Brujah or Cappadocious, isn't he?<br /> <br /> He is not perfect, that's the point. He is deeply flawed and his greatest strenght, ambition, is also his weakness, but he is really some kind of Miltonian hero, like Satan in Paradise Lost.<br /> &quot;Better to rule in Hell than serve in Heaven&quot;, I doubt anyone would agree more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 09-18-2019, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T09:47:44-07:00","id":1336580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336571#post1336571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>His whole story is quite an interesting one. For me, that's because he embodies the old trope I've seen in plenty of old stories where &quot;the little guy triumphs over adversity and becomes a great figure&quot; - but without doing the tired old thing of having it happen through moral goodness that would realistically get him killed a hundred times over.<br /> <br /> He's certainly many steps above Augustus &quot;be the biggest asshole in the world for no reason and then end that world for ill-thought-out reasons, hahaha I'm rich!&quot; Giovanni.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25611-gilbythefat","name":"GilbyTheFat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25611_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:28:20-07:00","id":1336697,"title":"","content":"Haqim's only regret is not knowing what regret feels like.<br /> Saulot once had an awkward moment, just to see how it feels.<br /> Tzimisce is left-handed and right-handed.<br /> Malkav is fluent in all languages, including three that he only speaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T04:31:27-07:00","id":1336820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336549#post1336549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well now you have me curious. What is your cannon explanation?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will post it on here at some point soon - I wanted to pinpoint what aspects of cannon I wanted to keep and what I wanted to change a little bit. It is largely in line with V20 thinking I think. I would post it now but I keep checking the forums when I am at work (I am a slacker) and don't have any of my stuff with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12180-jeevesosiris","name":"Jeevesosiris","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T13:06:21-07:00","id":1482022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeevesosiris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1336820#post1336820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I will post it on here at some point soon - I wanted to pinpoint what aspects of cannon I wanted to keep and what I wanted to change a little bit. It is largely in line with V20 thinking I think. I would post it now but I keep checking the forums when I am at work (I am a slacker) and don't have any of my stuff with me.</div> </div> </div> </div>3 years later and i am still waiting for your explanation lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T17:24:11-07:00","id":1482036,"title":"","content":"I guess it's easier for me to say which were least interesting. But all are or were interesting, and absolutely all of them had the potential (but we knew close to nothing of them).<br /> <br /> So...<br /> Arikel, Ennoia, Ravana and Ventru or Vidarta. Just because we got sooo little from them. Set almost steps into this one, but mostly because of the simplistic way he is so many times portrayed, especially as &quot;the egyptianesque evil guy&quot;. And well, 2nd generation is boring as hell cuz we know nothing of them, and it is no problem for me. Caine is absolutely interesting, and even profound, and I like the myth potential he has, but being the key-axis of it all, it is better for him to remain myth, and nothing factual about him exists.<br /> <br /> But the Antes I most like would be Haqim and Saulot and Tzimisce (my name kind of gave the answer some). They have very interesting parallels and searches. It is a shame Malkav and Troile or Brujah did not had more interactions with them. And I have a reaally soft spot for Cappadocius, the madman, cuz his plan is awesome, and really sounds well-intentioned, but crazy. So running Giovanni Chronciles, I will make the PCs see that the dude they conspired and helped to kill, especially his son (Japphet) knew and was doing much more than it seemed. They were really ignorant and playing with things MUCH bigger than they could ever imagine. <br /> <br /> I would like to know more of Arikel and Ennoia cuz their clans end up being so much of the same that they could show more depth to them. Besides they are the few female Antes (at the very least that are not contested most of the time). Ventru just... could be awesome, but nah, he just POOFED outside of the walls of the 2nd City and nobody knows who (just that supposedly wasn't Brujah/ Troile). Ravana we just don't know nothing, and Set we get just a retelling of the Egyptian myth with vamps and more mummies in the middle most of the time.<br /> <br /> Lots of wasted or fizzled potential (or room for myths).<br /> I loved the Cult of the Blood Gods approach. Cuz that is as much as we should get, but there should be something.<br /> Irad (Cult of the same name) and Zilah (Lost Tribe) have fun followings with interesting proceedings. And I don't care for any facts about the &quot;original&quot; characters if they indeed were more than myth, but some stories and constructions (I mean, text, character, anecdotes, stories, sayings...) around them would be nice.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T17:45:15-07:00","id":1482041,"title":"","content":"Saulot was set up as having his fingers in a lot of pies over the course of Vampire: the Dark Ages and Vampire Revised Edition, and I was never satisfied with the &quot;oops, I'm good now&quot; denouement of the Iconnu and Gehenna books. One of the most cowardly wastes of potential in the history of the game line. I don't believe he got the ending he deserved.<br /> <br /> The same goes for &quot;Set? Set's dead. Set's always been dead. Forever. What 2nd Edition?&quot;<br /> <br /> Ennoia. Almost certainly the first Cainite to leave the cities and strike out on her own, almost certainly the first to circumnavigate the globe; the story that she ended up choosing to dissolve far enough into the earth that she couldn't be reached and sleep away eternity has been told in so many sources that she's one of the very few Antediluvians whose fates I'd consider canon. She strikes me as a tragic and lonely creature.<br /> <br /> Arikel seems to have never caused any trouble, with every legend about her casting her as just this travelling bon vivant. She's probably active in the Modern Nights, blending in, loving humanity and receiving love in turn. She probably has wonderful stories to tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-27-2022, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T18:12:39-07:00","id":1482044,"title":"","content":"I agree with you about Ennoia and Arikel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T20:14:17-07:00","id":1482047,"title":"","content":"Not so sure about Ennoia's fate being tragic. She can feed on any vampire who is earth-melded, so she never wants for food. She is extremely safe. She has antedeluvian level Animalism so she can enjoy all of nature at once. Ennoia won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T20:46:13-07:00","id":1482049,"title":"","content":"A whole load of Giovanni seems to have gathered here. Maybe I can learn something about Necromancy?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I find that different Antes are in various degree of interesting depending on how I'm feeling. Right now [Brujah] is interesting to me but as I move on, someone else will probably take that slot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T07:58:04-07:00","id":1482073,"title":"","content":"I find Venture to be the most interesting mainly due to the Indian venture bloodline that seem to practice a type of blood magic known as Sadhana. Sadhana revolves around reincarnation and fate, which means the Venture ante may have been an experienced Sadhana practitioner, making him an expert in reincarnation. This leads me to theorize that the venture ante let himself die so he could enter the wheel of reincarnation for an unspecified goal.<br /> <br /> Is this a weak theory? Yeah it is.<br /> <br /> Did I come up with it because Sadhana is my favorite type of blood magic? 100% yes.<br /> <br /> Could their be any legitimacy behind it? Def not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T08:53:55-07:00","id":1482074,"title":"","content":"The only one that interests me is Set... well, maybe the Ravnos antediluvian too. <br /> <br /> Is the antediluvian the same guy as the god of the clan? Just a Gangrel progenitor of a bloodline turned clan whose story got muddled up with the holy purpose they found (or which found them?)? Is he dead? Is that how he got to the bottom of the Underworld where that fight with a giant snake of entropy and darkness supposedly happened? Is he just AWOL? How many &quot;Sets&quot; are there, really? There's so much fun to be had with the origin of the Setites.<br /> <br /> On the Ravnos' side, what's going on with this clan and the Dreaming? Like, their discipline manipulates chimera and the Dreaming, they hunt changelings and take their territory and stuff. I get the war with 1000 demons thing, but that's usually taken as refering to the wan gui, how did <i>this</i> develop? How did they develop a discipline linked to a layer of reality usually limited to changelings? Zapathasura, Ravnos, whatever your name is, what was your life??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T11:12:11-07:00","id":1482083,"title":"","content":"I'm fond of the contradictions and mystery of the Brujah antediuvian and what really happened to him or her. On one hand you have a cold callous dispassionate and learned scholar and then on the other you have a strongly passionate and easily angered person who is also incredibly learned. Is Brujah having a long psychological melt down?<br /> <br /> Tzismice is another one who kinds of interests me as a person who seeks out incredible lore and not care about the repurcussions and seeks to surpass it's &quot;peers&quot; and how it pulled a fast one on it's &quot;family&quot;.<br /> <br /> Malkav for what did he learn to shatter his mind.<br /> <br /> Set. What does he really want and is what his clan is fed the real truth?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-28-2022, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T12:02:20-07:00","id":1482091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482083#post1482083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm found of the contradictions and mystery of the Brujah antediuvian and what really happened to him or her. On one hand you have a cold callous dispassionate and learned scholar and then on the other you have a strongly passionate and easily angered person who is also incredibly learned. Is Brujah having a long psychological melt down?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my suspicion as well: that the Brujah/Troile story is complete B.S. and Brujah just spent a long time repressing his emotions, one just couldn't do it anymore, changed so much he seemed like a different person, and this Jekyll/Hyde change became a myth of his destruction.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T14:52:08-07:00","id":1482105,"title":"","content":"I don't find any of the individual Antedeluvians interesting because we're never told anything interesting about them. They're ciphers. At best, they are some kind of archetype of impending doom. But as &quot;characters&quot; they're, at best, stock characters.<br /> <br /> To make them interesting, we'd need some kind of idea what it is they intend to do during Gehenna, how they relate and interact with the other characters in the Jyhad, and some kind of real personality. The game doesn't provide those, and I've never seen STs provide that (or if they do, it's so bad it would have been better if they didn't).<br /> <br /> At best, we're given some limited information on &quot;why they let themselves be diablerized&quot; or &quot;how they faked their diablerization&quot; which falls short of real characterization.<br /> <br /> I don't count the 3rd generation pretenders that founded their own clan (Tremere and Giovanni) because those are much closer to actual characters much closer to the modern day and have discernible motives. They're not actual antedeluvians, just children playing with matches inside a tinderbox thinking they are masters.<br /> <br /> I don't think that's actually a problem. I find &quot;the Antedeluvians&quot; <i>as a collective</i> to be interesting. They are meant to be mysteries, and the role they play are meant to be unknown and terrifying. They're the monsters under the bed for vampires who normally play that role to mortals. And as ostensible survivors for an antedeluvian world before the Deluge or some other cataclysm, they represent an age of legend that is now now lost to us. In almost every case where the publisher showed us something about one of the antedeluvians, I was always rather unimpressed as it didn't meet my own expectations of dread and grandiosity. I find it mostly pedestrian and unimaginative when it isn't ridiculous (like what they did with Tzimisce) This is achievable - I've read lots of works that dealt in similar themes and have been blown away. That's why I steal liberally from Mike Mignola, Robert E. Howard, Biblical apocrypha, real world crackpot theories, and many others when I try to conjure my own ideas on what to possibly do with the Jyhad or revelations about Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:08:40-07:00","id":1482145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482044#post1482044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with you about Ennoia and Arikel.</div> </div> </div> </div>anyone find it odd/annoying that these are the only two Clan founders understood (consistently) by their Clan to be women? And even if I drop \u201cconsistently\u201d, that just means adding Troile (who I tend to actually interpret either as a trans man or gender-queer). So 2-3 out of 13+","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T06:31:28-07:00","id":1482147,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea, Troile was not sucessfull and was eaten by his/her sire, and with a bit of reverse-mithras, the passionate youngster affected the old passionless antediluvian; the Brujah Antediluvan assumed the identity of Troile to live escape the life he created for himself as &quot;Brujah&quot; to live out everything he &quot;missed&quot; while been a geek to a point, he maybe actually belived himself to be Troile<br /> But the Ilyes version is nice too with Temporis and all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T07:26:41-07:00","id":1482155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482145#post1482145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> anyone find it odd/annoying that these are the only two Clan founders understood (consistently) by their Clan to be women? And even if I drop \u201cconsistently\u201d, that just means adding Troile (who I tend to actually interpret either as a trans man or gender-queer). So 2-3 out of 13+</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would it be odd? Antes were made over 10,000 years ago. Women werent exactly held in high regard back then. In fact, i would sooner argue that it is odd that 2-3 of them are women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 05-28-2022, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:18:39-07:00","id":1482162,"title":"","content":"In regards to Trolie. Nobody really knows what this person gender was and most these ancient monsters have been said to be no longer concerned with such notions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:36:05-07:00","id":1482164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482155#post1482155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would it be odd? Antes were made over 10,000 years ago. Women werent exactly held in high regard back then. In fact, i would sooner argue that it is odd that 2-3 of them are women.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I beg to differ<br /> Women in ancient Sumer could buy, own, sell, and inherit property. They could engage in commerce and testify in court as witnesses<br /> In ancient Egypt, women enjoyed the same rights under the law as a man, they were legally equal to men (weel as much as they could be in a society dominated by men and was patriarchal in nature)<br /> Women in India during the early Vedic period enjoyed equal status with men in all aspects of life<br /> Back to prehistoric periods, for a long time the common assumption was that prehistoric men hunted while women gathered and reared their young. But for decades, some scholars have argued that these \u201ctraditional\u201d roles\u2014documented by anthropologists studying hunter-gatherer groups across the globe since the 19th century\u2014don\u2019t necessarily stretch into our deep past. Randall Haas, an archaeologist at University of California, in 2018 with his team of researchers gathered around the excavated burial of an individual lain to rest in the Andes Mountains of Peru some 9,000 years ago. Along with the bones of what appeared to be a human adult was an impressive\u2014and extensive\u2014kit of stone tools an ancient hunter would need to take down big game, from engaging the hunt to preparing the hide. Further analysis revealed a surprise: the remains found alongside the toolkit were from a biological female. What's more, this ancient female hunter was likely not an anomaly, according the studies. The Haas team\u2019s find was followed by a review of previously studied burials of similar age throughout the Americas\u2014and it revealed that between 30 and 50 percent of big game hunters could have been biologically female.<br /> Thanks to the latest stuides, it is now clear, during Prehistoric times, women also hunted large mammals, painted cave walls and practiced warfare and their equality and improtance continued to the later ages and inequality is just a few thousand years old &quot;new trend&quot;<br /> But back when V:tM came out we knew a bit less about these things, thus the few female Antediluvans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T09:59:41-07:00","id":1482167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482155#post1482155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Why would it be odd? Antes were made over 10,000 years ago. Women werent exactly held in high regard back then. In fact, i would sooner argue that it is odd that 2-3 of them are women.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019re confusing the Neolithic period with much much later eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T10:31:54-07:00","id":1482169,"title":"","content":"The time frame for the First City and the Flood are enough of a grey area that nearly any values assumed to be held by that society should be understood as just as made up. (The legends told by a number of independent clans don't even include that story, at all.)<br /> <br /> Looking at the commonly accepted (but again, really just assumed) genders of the thirteen who supposedly survived the flood and went on to found the clans, one could extrapolate an idea of what kind of gender politics their sires practiced. Why not? It could even be a plot point, the subject of theological debate between Noddists and Bahari, or a revenge motive for a wakening Methusaleh.<br /> <br /> If it feels like there's something there, it can always be used, even if it's an example of where the founders proved fallible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T17:56:31-07:00","id":1482428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482145#post1482145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> anyone find it odd/annoying that these are the only two Clan founders understood (consistently) by their Clan to be women? And even if I drop \u201cconsistently\u201d, that just means adding Troile (who I tend to actually interpret either as a trans man or gender-queer). So 2-3 out of 13+</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T18:40:55-07:00","id":1482880,"title":"","content":"Set, at least he's redheaded, lol and we actually know how he look like, unlike most Antediluvian that we have basically no idea of how they would look like. I think that it would be interesting to have a better description of the Antediluvians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T07:54:16-07:00","id":1482929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482145#post1482145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> anyone find it odd/annoying that these are the only two Clan founders understood (consistently) by their Clan to be women? And even if I drop \u201cconsistently\u201d, that just means adding Troile (who I tend to actually interpret either as a trans man or gender-queer). So 2-3 out of 13+</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying that you want the group collectively known for being spiteful, canabalistic assholes and the root of a large chunk of the worlds suffering to have more female representaion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T09:07:37-07:00","id":1482936,"title":"","content":"The interesting Antediluvians are the ones who actually do stuff. This puts Cappadocius and Saulot high on the list, as they have probably done the most especially recently. The Nosferatu Antediluvian with his obsession over his appearance and efforts to destroy his own Clan is also interesting. Tzimisce and what ever it has become is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T10:29:35-07:00","id":1482945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482929#post1482929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you saying that you want the group collectively known for being spiteful, canabalistic assholes and the root of a large chunk of the worlds suffering to have more female representaion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes? Why wouldn\u2019t I? Ancient mythology is full of powerful goddesses, sorceries queens, and mothers of monsters who are as immoral as their male counterparts by the standards of modern values","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T10:36:35-07:00","id":1482947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482936#post1482936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting Antediluvians are the ones who actually do stuff. This puts Cappadocius and Saulot high on the list, as they have probably done the most especially recently. The Nosferatu Antediluvian with his obsession over his appearance and efforts to destroy his own Clan is also interesting. Tzimisce and what ever it has become is interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my book, the only thing Saulot and Cappadocian have been doing recently is being dead. What they had done excellently","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T11:52:28-07:00","id":1482956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482945#post1482945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes? Why wouldn\u2019t I? Ancient mythology is full of powerful goddesses, sorceries queens, and mothers of monsters who are as immoral as their male counterparts by the standards of modern values</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm asking because I don't understand Why it's particularly necessary and it rings to me like when the internet was up in arms about how the world needs more female dictators. I'm caught between wondering why you would want that group to &quot;represent&quot; any collection of people you like and why that particular group needs to represent anyone in particular.<br /> <br /> It's not like WoD is hurting in any sort of representation either. The setting was making badass women in politics, non-binary heroes/villains, and characters of every race since the 90's. The WoD already Has badass female goddesses sorceries queens, and mothers of monsters(the struggle between the Weaver and Gaia, both being goddesses, in WtA has flat out been stated by the writers as more important in the long run than the wyrm issue the werewolves are focusing on).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T12:09:32-07:00","id":1482957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482956#post1482956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm asking because I don't understand Why it's particularly necessary and it rings to me like when the internet was up in arms about how the world needs more female dictators. I'm caught between wondering why you would want that group to &quot;represent&quot; any collection of people you like and why that particular group needs to represent anyone in particular.<br /> <br /> It's not like WoD is hurting in any sort of representation either. The setting was making badass women in politics, non-binary heroes/villains, and characters of every race since the 90's. The WoD already Has badass female goddesses sorceries queens, and mothers of monsters(the struggle between the Weaver and Gaia, both being goddesses, in WtA has flat out been stated by the writers as more important in the long run than the wyrm issue the werewolves are focusing on).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a fundamental difference between real people and fictional characters, so this comparison with dictators isn't really significant. A fictional character arises from a conscious decision by the author and can be called on that basis.<br /> <br /> It is also worth of note that representation isn't only about being linked to the &quot;good stuff&quot;, so to speak, but about recognizing human potential. Whenever a characters group lacks representation, it begs to question what may be implied there, by design or not. It isn't and has never been only about &quot;claiming the good stuff&quot;, but being recognized as equally diverse and ambitious.<br /> <br /> Not that I specifically have a problem with the current canon on the Antes, because the current canon has a lot of assumptions that are not strictly confirmed, so most of them may be depicted as males just because the people telling their stories expect them to be so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T12:45:55-07:00","id":1482961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482957#post1482957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I specifically have a problem with the current canon on the Antes, because the current canon has a lot of assumptions that are not strictly confirmed, so most of them may be depicted as males just because the people telling their stories expect them to be so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, about the Ante's gender itself isn't what I have misgivings about, just the idea that characters and stories need to be retroactively changed to fit the current politics. I'm probably just having a knee jerk reaction after seeing so many franchises I liked die on the alter of representation.<br /> <br /> Trying to change major aspects of the setting's history to represent our current political climate rubs me the wrong way. It can definitely have our current politics if done well and treated maturely, WoD is a game About politics after all, but I've seen it done wrong Way too often lately.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T14:33:06-07:00","id":1482968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482947#post1482947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my book, the only thing Saulot and Cappadocian have been doing recently is being dead. What they had done excellently</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How interesting! Would you care to tell me more about your book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T14:47:37-07:00","id":1482969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482961#post1482961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, about the Ante's gender itself isn't what I have misgivings about, just the idea that characters and stories need to be retroactively changed to fit the current politics. I'm probably just having a knee jerk reaction after seeing so many franchises I liked die on the alter of representation.<br /> <br /> Trying to change major aspects of the setting's history to represent our current political climate rubs me the wrong way. It can definitely have our current politics if done well and treated maturely, WoD is a game About politics after all, but I've seen it done wrong Way too often lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>i didn\u2019t mention anything about changing anything in future published books, so this is your baggage that is irrelevant to the discussion being had about how the unconscious social biases of the original writers shaping the setting in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T15:08:44-07:00","id":1482973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482961#post1482961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trying to change major aspects of the setting's history to represent our current political climate rubs me the wrong way. It can definitely have our current politics if done well and treated maturely, WoD is a game About politics after all, but I've seen it done wrong Way too often lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, Classic VtM books, to my knowledge, were presented with UNRELIABLE narrators. That by itself encourages, if not inevitably mandates, &quot;retroactive changes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Perhaps more importantly, expecting the setting NOT to change to match &quot;the current political climate,&quot; is like expecting people in the 90s to still want to watch westerns from the 60s.<br /> <br /> The elephant in the room is that modern people are not going to want to play something with politics from &quot;the war on terror,&quot; or further back. And these people have JUST as MUCH a right to take their business elsewhere as the game devs have a right to &quot;preserve decades of canon,&quot; or &quot;honor the original author's intent.&quot;<br /> <br /> When the Wheel of Time series came out, I didn't go venting or chastising them for updating the politics of a series that started more than three decades ago, I just went and read the original books again. You can't just expect things to not change just because it's not convenient for you.<br /> <br /> &quot;The 90s are over.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 06-03-2022, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T15:14:52-07:00","id":1482974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The interesting Antediluvians are the ones who actually do stuff. </div> </div> </div>I also share this vision and as such, on a serious note, even though Set is a redhead, I'd consider Tremere, Saulot and Cappadocius high on the list, merely for being very active. Tzimisce, I like as well but I feel the writers sometimes made him a bit &quot;over the top&quot;, it's sometimes implied that the guy (or the <i>thing</i>) is the most powerful being in the WoD and I feel it's a bit too much.<br /> If I'm not mistaken, Tremere has dark brown or black hair, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T15:38:13-07:00","id":1482979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482974#post1482974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also share this vision and as such, on a serious note, even though Set is a redhead, I'd consider Tremere, Saulot and Cappadocius high on the list, merely for being very active. Tzimisce, I like as well but I feel the writers sometimes made him a bit &quot;over the top&quot;, it's sometimes implied that the guy (or the <i>thing</i>) is the most powerful being in the WoD and I feel it's a bit too much.<br /> If I'm not mistaken, Tremere has dark brown or black hair, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When was the eldest implied to be the most powerful being in wod?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T15:41:23-07:00","id":1482981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482974#post1482974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also share this vision and as such, on a serious note, even though Set is a redhead, I'd consider Tremere, Saulot and Cappadocius high on the list, merely for being very active. Tzimisce, I like as well but I feel the writers sometimes made him a bit &quot;over the top&quot;, it's sometimes implied that the guy (or the <i>thing</i>) is the most powerful being in the WoD and I feel it's a bit too much.<br /> If I'm not mistaken, Tremere has dark brown or black hair, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Transylvania Chronicles does have a scene with him showing up just to dab and stick the PCs in the mud. Don't remember if they describe the man. But I do love one portrait of him in one of the exclusive german supplement which is a clean-shaven, white-eyed, middle to old aged man, looking so darn powerful with just a look and a stare, with flowing long white or gray hair (although it could be fair). But, it is just an illustration, and White Wolf was never too concise with those. <br /> <br /> And I think Cappadocius plans and Augustus Giovanni succesful plan of Giovanni dominance and independance are also very interesting!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T16:01:26-07:00","id":1482984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482961#post1482961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, about the Ante's gender itself isn't what I have misgivings about, just the idea that characters and stories need to be retroactively changed to fit the current politics. I'm probably just having a knee jerk reaction after seeing so many franchises I liked die on the alter of representation.<br /> <br /> Trying to change major aspects of the setting's history to represent our current political climate rubs me the wrong way. It can definitely have our current politics if done well and treated maturely, WoD is a game About politics after all, but I've seen it done wrong Way too often lately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand what you mean, but first the problem is that to have a mature discussion about this we need a mature reception to this. In the sense that, when you simply take the opposite stance and start to argue that the change shouldn't happen, you just help to polarize thoughts and lead to the immature reactions that lead to immature developments, be them in whichever direction.<br /> <br /> R.I.P. Gender Bender Ghostbusters, really wished you ended up a good movie. You didn't.<br /> <br /> But for the matter at hand, this is one of the situations where you can't really hurt much of the established setting with this. All we like to discuss a lot about them taking what's said about them at face value, the fact is that the setting primarily treats Antediluvians as legends, everything said being said by someone within it with limited knowledge and bias. Most of them have assumed genders when all witnesses to their very existence, if there's any, came into the picture already so late that even identifying sex or gender was hard or impossible. It hardly plays any role, either, with very few exceptions.<br /> <br /> So here we have it, adding stories and theories about the Antes that contradict with the previous ones isn't just possible, it is actually how the setting is supposed to work. With that, it isn't hard to implement representation and diversity to the story while improving it without negating previous statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482974#post1482974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also share this vision and as such, on a serious note, even though Set is a redhead, I'd consider Tremere, Saulot and Cappadocius high on the list, merely for being very active. Tzimisce, I like as well but I feel the writers sometimes made him a bit &quot;over the top&quot;, it's sometimes implied that the guy (or the <i>thing</i>) is the most powerful being in the WoD and I feel it's a bit too much.<br /> If I'm not mistaken, Tremere has dark brown or black hair, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a rule of thumb we shouldn't pack Tremere and Augustus with the Antes. Not just because they're not technically so, as they're far younger, but because they play very differently in the lore. They're very active, well known and directly described, as there are several eye witnesses to them.<br /> <br /> Tremere in particular for being older than 1st edition as a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T18:46:08-07:00","id":1483002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482961#post1482961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, about the Ante's gender itself isn't what I have misgivings about, just the idea that characters and stories need to be retroactively changed to fit the current politics. I'm probably just having a knee jerk reaction after seeing so many franchises I liked die on the alter of representation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Been a while since I posted here, and it'll probably be a while still after, but I have to say; I find this take a bit strange for VtM.<br /> <br /> Vampire's setting has always bent and twisted its past around current politics, current trends and the current climate. V5 is literally the WoD through a 9/11 lens. VtM1e and 2e was cemented in a world where Anne Rice and the X-Files universes were the norm, with secret conspiracies and historical figures mixing with each other on the regular, where major wars were smokescreens for undead politics... until Revised literally undid that to make kindred have a smaller impact, around the time inevitable nihilism in the face of inevitable apocalypses captured the zeitgeist of pop culture.<br /> <br /> VtM has long been retaining itself to keep up with politics and trends. Having the in-universe mythological monsters with genders other than Male and Token Female is actually less of a change than we've already seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T19:09:19-07:00","id":1483004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As a rule of thumb we shouldn't pack Tremere and Augustus with the Antes. Not just because they're not technically so, as they're far younger, but because they play very differently in the lore. They're very active, well known and directly described, as there are several eye witnesses to them. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I know, but I feel the need to add them for simplicity's sake as they're &quot;systematically Antediluvian&quot;, so to speak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tremere in particular for being older than 1st edition as a character. </div> </div> </div>Also yes, this in particular is one of the reasons why I think the Clan Tremere is one of the best developed in WoD, besides the hate they usually get from the &quot;average Joe the Brujah, but only Celerity and Potence please&quot;. In general, I wish we had more of an imagery of the Antediluvian and more actions attributed to them, funny enough, Gehenna didn't do much in this regard, even though it seemed this was one of the intentions behind the books. We need more novels!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 06-04-2022, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T20:03:32-07:00","id":1483006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1482984#post1482984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule of thumb we shouldn't pack Tremere and Augustus with the Antes. Not just because they're not technically so, as they're far younger, but because they play very differently in the lore. They're very active, well known and directly described, as there are several eye witnesses to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, that that metric also describes both Cappadocius and Saulot. They were also very active, very well known, directly described and there were numerous eye witnesses who interacted with them. I've always found it interesting how they were also, coincidently (or perhaps not?) the only two antes that were diablarized and had their clans functionally replaced (perhaps the Brujah/Trujah fall into that as well though?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-03T22:01:24-07:00","id":1483012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1335692-most-interesting-antediluvian?p=1483006#post1483006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, that that metric also describes both Cappadocius and Saulot. They were also very active, very well known, directly described and there were numerous eye witnesses who interacted with them. I've always found it interesting how they were also, coincidently (or perhaps not?) the only two antes that were diablarized and had their clans functionally replaced (perhaps the Brujah/Trujah fall into that as well though?)</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but here's where being an Ante by age plays a rile. They're all interesting characters, but while Tremere and Augustus distinguish themselves for raising up fairly recently, not even being Methuselah yet, Cappadocius and Saulot distinguish themselves <i>despite it</i>. That's a point that I think to be worth attention enough to justify not packing them together.<br /> <br /> Depending on how you look at the definition of Methuselah and read their actions, it could be said that at least Saulot and Cappadocius among the Antes never made the change. They're extremely old Elders, but never became true Methuselahs. They're also the two that we know to possibly be trying to leave the Jyhad entirely without need to rely to legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}